{
  "dom_id": "step-q280515",
  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "A parcel robot begins at the position ${r}_{0}=(3i+2j)\\,\\text{cm}$ with an initial velocity of $(i-j)\\,\\text{cm/s}$ and a constant acceleration of $(2i+j)\\,{\\text{cm/s}}^{2}.$ Determine the position vector after $3$ seconds.\n\n$r=(${{field-1}}\n$i\\,\\,+$\n{{field-2}}\n$j)\\text{cm}$",
  "worked_solution": "If a particle moves with constant acceleration $a,$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut+\\frac{1}{2}a{t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle and $u$ is its initial velocity.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=3i+2j,\\,u=i-j,\\,a=2i+j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the parcel robot after $t=3\\,\\text{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =(3i+2j)+(i-j)(3)+\\frac{1}{2}(2i+j)(3)^{2} \\\\  & =(3i+2j)+(i-j)(3)+\\frac{1}{2}(18i+9j) \\\\  & =(3i+2j)+(3i-3j)+(9i+4.5j) \\\\  & =(\\,15\\,i+3.5\\,j)\\,\\text{cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
